# fig_prop_check

**Claim carried:** C1: the excess width of PPI++ and of the calibrated estimators over the floor equals the closed-form prediction; the exactly affine case sits at zero.

**Shows:** predicted (x) against measured (y) excess width over the estimated floor, one point per cell and estimator (filled = synthetic cell, hollow centre = real dataset; estimators without a closed form are not drawn), with the Monte-Carlo CI of the measurement; dashed line = identity.

**How to read:** points on the dashed line within their CI mean the formula holds in that cell; points off it are cells where it does not.

